# CODEOWNERS — ownership map for auth-separation (AUTH-001)
#
# Maps each service directory and each specification to a named owner, so that a change to a
# contract or a service pulls in the right reviewer automatically.
#
# NOTE ON ENFORCEMENT: this file only *requests* review. It becomes a gate only when branch
# protection on `main` enables "Require review from Code Owners" — a repository-administration
# setting that cannot be committed from a working tree. Until that is switched on, treat the
# entries below as documentation of intent.
#
# The Kanban assigns notional teams per ticket (Platform engineering, Security engineering,
# Identity, Data). This repository has a single real owner, so every path resolves to that owner;
# split these lines into teams if and when the work is staffed that way.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                       @GBrooks1970

# --- Specifications: the reviewed deliverable. Changes here are contract changes. -------------
/specs/                 @GBrooks1970
/features/              @GBrooks1970

# --- Services: each directory is owned alongside the contract that governs it. ----------------
/services/authn/        @GBrooks1970
/services/authz/        @GBrooks1970
/services/userinfo/     @GBrooks1970

# --- Infrastructure and CI: deployment topology, secrets wiring, the spec-validation gate. ----
/infra/                 @GBrooks1970
/.github/               @GBrooks1970
/scripts/               @GBrooks1970

